 "text": "Recorder of Deeds | Marion County, Missouri\nSkip to content\nUpcoming Events\nFacebook\nMarion County, Missouri\nServices\nCalendar\nEconomic Development\nEmployment\nCareers\nMarriage License\nMilitary Discharge\nVoting\nDepartments\nAssessor\nSenior Real Estate Property Tax Relief Program\nCircuit Clerk District 1\nCircuit Clerk District 2\nCollector of Revenue\nCommission\nCoroner\nCounty Clerk\nElection Results\nCounty Coordinator\nEmergency Management\nHighway Department\nMU Extension\nProsecuting Attorney\nBad Checks & Restitution\nCase Information & Links\nCriminal Prosecution\nVictim Advocate\nPublic Administrator\nUseful Links\nRecorder of Deeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nForms\nHelpful Links\nServices\nCalendar\nEconomic Development\nEmployment\nCareers\nMarriage License\nMilitary Discharge\nVoting\nDepartments\nAssessor\nSenior Real Estate Property Tax Relief Program\nCircuit Clerk District 1\nCircuit Clerk District 2\nCollector of Revenue\nCommission\nCoroner\nCounty Clerk\nElection Results\nCounty Coordinator\nEmergency Management\nHighway Department\nMU Extension\nProsecuting Attorney\nBad Checks & Restitution\nCase Information & Links\nCriminal Prosecution\nVictim Advocate\nPublic Administrator\nUseful Links\nRecorder of Deeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nForms\nHelpful Links\nRecorder of Deeds\nWhat We Do\nThe responsibility of the Recorder of Deeds office is to file for record, maintain, and preserve all the land records of Marion County. Marriage license records and military discharge papers are also filed in this office.\nDo you have questions about what Recorders do? View the Recorders’ Association of Missouri (RAM) video on the history and functions of the Recorder of Deeds.\nOnline Records\nView official records online\nProperty Fraud Alerts\nVisit the Property Fraud Alert Service\nRecorder's Fees\nReal Estate\nStandard Document: $26 for the first page (8 1/2 x 11 inches); $3 for each additional page thereafter.\nNon-Standard Document: $25 penalty fee.\nAdditional Fees: $5 for each additional referenced document.\nPlats: $46 for the first page (18 x 24 inches); $25 for each additional page thereafter.\n24″ x 36″ or larger – $71.00 For each additional page – $50.00\nSurveys: $26 for the first page (18 x 24 inches); $5 for each additional page thereafter. $31 for the first page (24 x 36 inches); $10 for each additional page thereafter.\nCopy of Real Estate Document: $2 for up to five pages; $0.25 for each additional page.\nCertified Copy of Real Estate Document: $3 for up to five pages; $0.25 for each additional page.\nAll requests for documents to be mailed must be accompanied by a self-addressed stamped envelope of sufficient size to accommodate the document.\nContact\nMain Office\n100 S. Main St., P.O. Box 392, Palmyra, Missouri 63461\nPhone: (573) 769-7001\nFax: (573) 769-6012\nEmail the Recorder of Deeds\nHarla Friesz\nRecorder of Deeds\nBusiness Hours\nMonday through Friday.\n8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.\nMarion County, Missouri\nOpen 8am-5pm, Mon-Fri\nAccessibility\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nSite Map\n© 2026 Marion County, Missouri. Website Designed by Poole Communications.",
